 [  Ok  ][  Cancel  ]

#Save outgoing messages# - turn on this option to save all outgoing
message in selected folder.

#Search for header...# - turn on this option if You want FARMail to
check for %start%..%end% block in Your outgoing messages.

#Try to resume...# - if You turn on this option, incomplete messages
will be saved on disk with a possibility to resume download.

#Take file date...# - turn on this option to set file date and time
to message date and time (for incoming mail).

#Scripts# - enter here filenames for new message script and reply-script.

#Charset and Table# - here You can specify up to 3 additional encodings.
Just write #correct# charset name (for example, ISO-8859-5) in "Charset"
field, and the #correct# name of FAR encoding table in "table" field
(for example, "ISO 8859-5 (Unix russian)"). Note that You can write only
first letters of table name, for example "ISO 8859-5".


